<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n24806" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">invŏcātus</span></b> ,
			a, um, adj.
		2. in-voco. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>Uncalled</i> (class.): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">imagines rerum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic. N. D. 1, 38, 108</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ego ad subsellia rei occurro,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					Fam. 8, 8, 1</span></i>
			.— </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>Uninvited</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">invocatus soleo esse in convivio,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plaut.
					Capt. 1, 1, 2</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ut mihi ... invocato sit locus semper,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Ter.
					Eun. 5, 9, 29</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">cotidie sic ei cena coquebatur, ut quos
					invocatos vidisset in foro, omnes devocaret,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Nep.
					Cim. 4, 3</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Vitr. 6, 8</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
